# Unit 12 单词



## flood
- **音标**: /flʌd/
- **词性**: n. v.
- **释义**: 洪水；泛滥；大量涌入
- **例句**: The flood destroyed many homes in the area.
- **近义词**: deluge, inundation, overflow
- **派生词**: flooding (n.)

## flourish
- **音标**: /ˈflɜːrɪʃ/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 繁荣；兴旺；挥舞
- **例句**: The business has flourished under new management.
- **近义词**: thrive, prosper, bloom
- **派生词**: flourishing (adj.)

## flow
- **音标**: /floʊ/
- **词性**: v. n.
- **释义**: 流动；流畅
- **例句**: The river flows through the city center.
- **近义词**: stream, pour, circulate
- **派生词**: flowing (adj.)

## fluent
- **音标**: /ˈfluːənt/
- **词性**: adj.
- **释义**: 流利的；流畅的
- **例句**: She is fluent in three languages.
- **近义词**: articulate, eloquent, smooth
- **派生词**: fluently (adv.), fluency (n.)

## focus
- **音标**: /ˈfoʊkəs/
- **词性**: n. v.
- **释义**: 焦点；集中
- **例句**: You need to focus on your studies.
- **近义词**: concentrate, center, attention
- **派生词**: focused (adj.), unfocused (adj.)

## forbid
- **音标**: /fərˈbɪd/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 禁止；不许
- **例句**: Smoking is forbidden in this building.
- **近义词**: prohibit, ban, prevent
- **派生词**: forbidden (adj.), forbidding (adj.)

## forecast
- **音标**: /ˈfɔːrkæst/
- **词性**: v. n.
- **释义**: 预测；预报
- **例句**: The weather forecast predicts rain tomorrow.
- **近义词**: predict, project, anticipate
- **派生词**: forecaster (n.)

## forge
- **音标**: /fɔːrdʒ/
- **词性**: v. n.
- **释义**: 锻造；伪造；建立
- **例句**: The two countries forged a strong alliance.
- **近义词**: create, falsify, establish
- **派生词**: forgery (n.), forger (n.)

## former
- **音标**: /ˈfɔːrmər/
- **词性**: adj. n.
- **释义**: 以前的；前者
- **例句**: The former president gave a speech at the event.
- **近义词**: previous, earlier, past
- **派生词**: formerly (adv.)

## formula
- **音标**: /ˈfɔːrmjələ/
- **词性**: n.
- **释义**: 公式；配方；方案
- **例句**: The mathematical formula is easy to remember.
- **近义词**: equation, recipe, method
- **派生词**: formulate (v.), formulation (n.)

## fortune
- **音标**: /ˈfɔːrtʃən/
- **词性**: n.
- **释义**: 命运；财富；运气
- **例句**: He made a fortune in the stock market.
- **近义词**: wealth, luck, destiny
- **派生词**: fortunate (adj.), fortunately (adv.), unfortunate (adj.)

## foster
- **音标**: /ˈfɔːstər/
- **词性**: v. adj.
- **释义**: 培养；促进；收养的
- **例句**: Schools should foster creativity in students.
- **近义词**: encourage, promote, nurture
- **派生词**: fosterage (n.)

## foundation
- **音标**: /faʊnˈdeɪʃn/
- **词性**: n.
- **释义**: 基础；基金会；建立
- **例句**: Education is the foundation of a successful career.
- **近义词**: base, basis, groundwork
- **派生词**: found (v.), founder (n.), fundamental (adj.)

## fraction
- **音标**: /ˈfrækʃn/
- **词性**: n.
- **释义**: 分数；小部分；片段
- **例句**: Only a fraction of the students passed the exam.
- **近义词**: portion, part, fragment
- **派生词**: fractional (adj.)

## fragment
- **音标**: /ˈfræɡmənt/
- **词性**: n. v.
- **释义**: 碎片；片段；使破碎
- **例句**: Fragments of glass were scattered on the floor.
- **近义词**: piece, bit, shard
- **派生词**: fragmentary (adj.), fragmentation (n.)

## framework
- **音标**: /ˈfreɪmwɜːrk/
- **词性**: n.
- **释义**: 框架；体系；结构
- **例句**: We need a framework for the new policy.
- **近义词**: structure, skeleton, system

## fraud
- **音标**: /frɔːd/
- **词性**: n.
- **释义**: 欺诈；骗子
- **例句**: He was convicted of financial fraud.
- **近义词**: deception, scam, swindle
- **派生词**: fraudulent (adj.), defraud (v.)

## frequent
- **音标**: /ˈfriːkwənt/
- **词性**: adj.
- **释义**: 频繁的；经常的
- **例句**: She is a frequent visitor to the museum.
- **近义词**: common, regular, habitual
- **派生词**: frequently (adv.), frequency (n.)

## friction
- **音标**: /ˈfrɪkʃn/
- **词性**: n.
- **释义**: 摩擦；摩擦力；冲突
- **例句**: There is friction between the two departments.
- **近义词**: conflict, tension, resistance
- **派生词**: frictional (adj.)

## frontier
- **音标**: /frʌnˈtɪr/
- **词性**: n.
- **释义**: 前沿；边界；新领域
- **例句**: Space is the final frontier for exploration.
- **近义词**: border, boundary, edge

## frustrate
- **音标**: /ˈfrʌstreɪt/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 使沮丧；挫败
- **例句**: The lack of progress frustrated the team.
- **近义词**: discourage, thwart, disappoint
- **派生词**: frustration (n.), frustrated (adj.), frustrating (adj.)

## fulfill
- **音标**: /fʊlˈfɪl/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 实现；履行；满足
- **例句**: She fulfilled her dream of becoming a doctor.
- **近义词**: achieve, accomplish, satisfy
- **派生词**: fulfillment (n.), fulfilled (adj.)

## function
- **音标**: /ˈfʌŋkʃn/
- **词性**: n. v.
- **释义**: 功能；作用；运转
- **例句**: The function of the heart is to pump blood.
- **近义词**: role, purpose, operate
- **派生词**: functional (adj.), malfunction (n.)

## fund
- **音标**: /fʌnd/
- **词性**: n. v.
- **释义**: 基金；资金；资助
- **例句**: The government will fund the research project.
- **近义词**: finance, sponsor, capital
- **派生词**: funding (n.), fundamental (adj.), fundamentally (adv.)

## fundamental
- **音标**: /ˌfʌndəˈmentl/
- **词性**: adj. n.
- **释义**: 基本的；根本的；基础
- **例句**: Honesty is a fundamental value in any relationship.
- **近义词**: basic, essential, primary
- **派生词**: fundamentally (adv.), fundamentalism (n.)

## furnish
- **音标**: /ˈfɜːrnɪʃ/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 提供；装备；布置家具
- **例句**: The apartment is fully furnished.
- **近义词**: provide, supply, equip
- **派生词**: furniture (n.), furnishings (n.)

## furthermore
- **音标**: /ˌfɜːrðərˈmɔːr/
- **词性**: adv.
- **释义**: 此外；而且
- **例句**: The plan is too expensive; furthermore, it is impractical.
- **近义词**: moreover, besides, in addition

## gain
- **音标**: /ɡeɪn/
- **词性**: v. n.
- **释义**: 获得；增加；利益
- **例句**: She gained valuable experience from the internship.
- **近义词**: obtain, acquire, earn
- **派生词**: gainful (adj.), gainfully (adv.)

## gap
- **音标**: /ɡæp/
- **词性**: n.
- **释义**: 缺口；差距；间隔
- **例句**: There is a growing gap between the rich and the poor.
- **近义词**: opening, difference, divide
- **派生词**: gapped (adj.), gaping (adj.)

## gather
- **音标**: /ˈɡæðər/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 聚集；收集；推断
- **例句**: People gathered in the square to celebrate.
- **近义词**: collect, assemble, accumulate
- **派生词**: gathering (n.)

## generate
- **音标**: /ˈdʒenəreɪt/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 产生；引起；发电
- **例句**: The project will generate thousands of jobs.
- **近义词**: produce, create, yield
- **派生词**: generation (n.), generator (n.), generative (adj.)
